WEBVTT

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.480
He'll be waiting again, he'll be sorry for us.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.250
Sheila, please.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.270
Doesn't that man think there's anything important

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:36.270
about getting married?

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.370
About getting married to me?

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.370
Then show yourself our guests.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.430
Our guests?

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:42.070
They're probably whistling through their fingers

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:43.270
and stamping their feet.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.390
If they're still here.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:45.430
Sheila, you mustn't.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:47.030
You mustn't, dear.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.030
Oh, a bridal bouquet.

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:51.680
Pretty thing, isn't it?

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.380
Hello.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:54.860
Where's the bridegroom?

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.770
Well, that's what I'd like to know.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:57.770
Where's the bridegroom?

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:00.000
No, no, no, no, no, no, dear.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.480
Calm yourself. You'll spoil everything.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.480
Think of those people downstairs.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.430
That's what I am thinking about.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:08.410
They came here to see a wedding, didn't they?

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.410
Well, they're going to see one.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.410
But you can't have a wedding without a bridegroom.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:14.410
There'll be a bridegroom. Who's downstairs?

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:16.300
Fred, George, get Henry for me.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.300
Henry? Henry who?

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.300
Henry Tuttle, my lawyer.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.300
But you don't need a lawyer.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.170
Oh, yes I do. Now you're going, am I?

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.130
Oh, I'm going.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:41.520
No bridegroom, eh?

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:58.770
What happened to Sheila? Come at once.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:00.920
What's wrong?

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.240
You've always gotten me out of gems before, haven't you, Henry?

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.200
Yeah, plenty of them.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.760
Well, this is the biggest one I was ever in and you've got to get me out of it.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:07.240
How?

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.200
Marry me.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.830
Oh, you can't do this! It's crazy!

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:10.390
I didn't marry!

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.150
Mother, this is my wedding, not yours.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.750
It's all very simple and you're an attorney.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.350
All you have to do is change the license.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:17.110
Now, you can't see your attorney's done!

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.110
This is horrible! Horrible!

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.790
Yeah, but what about Eric?

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.080
Are you going to argue or marry me?

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.310
Are you serious?

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:26.900
Do I look playful?

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.160
Give me that little license.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:45.880
I'll be waiting at the church, Willie.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:04.590
How are you doing?

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:05.750
Oh, all right.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.020
Oh, no, isn't that silly?

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:09.800
Well, it's not so silly.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.240
That's an old custom that has a great deal of significance.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:13.580
Well, it's silly to me.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:15.310
Anyway, it's all over, thank goodness.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:15.790
Right.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.900
You know, I never thought I'd be lucky enough to manage this.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.580
Oh, you were wonderful, really.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:22.120
Except for a little nervousness.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.420
Now, I'm very grateful, Henry.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.880
Eric would have shown up eventually, but this will teach him a lesson.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:28.790
Next time, he'll be more punctual.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:29.930
Next time?

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.760
Yes. Oh, would you put this over here?

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:36.590
No.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:41.690
I won't be so lenient with you.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:46.170
I may be a little bit stupid, but just where does our marriage fit into this picture?

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:51.480
Oh, our marriage is a purely social gesture to save a purely social situation.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:05:00.000
See, bridegroom fails to show, I double for bridegroom, save your face, and help teach bridegroom to be a better boy hereafter.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:04.520
Exactly. I wouldn't be surprised if Eric took a plane and came right down after us.

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:10.510
Just how long you calculate you'll need my services as a stand-in.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:17.190
Oh, not long. As soon as the publicity dies down, I'll go to Reno and do it all very quietly.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:19.170
Everything will be straightened out for everybody.

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:21.220
You could choose a vacation, Henry.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:24.100
Oh, here it is.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:25.090
